export anchor GroupedDataGridStyle:
    number: 179
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Grouped data grid
    idea: The dashboard is one hierarchical grid, projects grouped under team header rows with subtotals, a sticky column header and inline progress strips, set in cool grey with a single teal accent.
    base: light
    palette:
        page: #eef1f2, the page behind panels
        surface: #ffffff, the top bar, panels and fields
        columnHead: #e6ebed, the sticky grid header row
        grid: #f6f8f8, row hover, the total row and the focused row
        ink: #1c2427, text
        muted: #4f5e65, labels, meta and column heads
        line: #d3dadd, panel edges and rules, with #e4e9eb for row rules
        slate: #7c8fa0, field edges and last week bars
        teal: #0f766e, the primary button, progress fills, this week bars, the current tab and focus
        tealTint: #e1f1ef, team group rows
        tealInk: #0b5c55, text on group rows and links
        green: #1d6b3c, On track
        amber: #8a5200, At risk
        red: #b3261e, Behind, the overdue figure and the overdue line
    type:
        One stack, system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica
        Neue, Arial, with tabular figures. KPI figures 22px at 650, the
        greeting 20px at 650, group rows 14px bold, cells 14px regular,
        column heads and panel titles 12 to 13px bold caps tracked 0.03
        to 0.04em, meta 12px.
    layout:
        A white top bar holds a small four square teal mark with the
        brand, a wide search field, then at right a teal New project
        button, a square bell with a red dot and the initials disc with
        Mara Okafor. Under it a row of text tabs, Home underlined in teal.
        The main area opens with one line holding the greeting, the date
        and a red clock with 4 tasks are overdue. Below sits a single
        bordered summary strip split into four cells by thin rules, each a
        figure beside its label, the overdue figure in red. Then two
        columns. The wide left panel is the grid titled Projects by team,
        with a grey sticky header row of Project, Status, Progress, Tasks,
        Due and Days left. Each team, Design, Engineering, Marketing and
        Research, has a teal tinted group row with a chevron, the project
        count, a subtotal progress strip and percent, done over total tasks
        and the next due date with its days left. Project rows are indented
        under it with the status word and shape, a 72px progress strip and
        percent, tasks, due date and days left. A grey All teams total row
        ends the grid with a teal sparkline of the 14 daily values, 46
        percent and 78 of 170. A status mix line under the grid counts 4
        On track, 1 At risk and 1 Behind. The 320px right column stacks a
        Tasks completed panel with 14 square bars, slate last week and teal
        this week, and an Activity panel as a two column table of time and
        sentence. Below 1060px the right column moves under the grid, and
        below 760px the grid scrolls sideways inside its panel with the
        project column pinned, the summary becomes two by two and the
        search takes its own row.
    spacing: An 8px unit. Cells are 7 by 12px, 16px between panels, a 24px page gutter.
    density: High. Every team, project, subtotal and total fits in one grid at 1280px.
    corners: 4px panels, 3px controls, square bars and strips.
    borders: 1px #d3dadd panel edges and #e4e9eb row rules, slate field edges, a teal 2px tab underline.
    shadows: None. Separation comes from lines and the teal tint on group rows.
    icons:
        Line icons at 1.8px stroke at text size in the header. Status
        shapes are filled at 13px beside the word, a check circle for On
        track, a triangle with a bang for At risk and a crossed square for
        Behind, plus a clock ring for overdue.
    focus: A 2px teal outline offset 1px. A focused field gets a teal border and outline, a focused row an inset outline on the grid grey.
    tone: Plain data labels, caps column heads and numbers before words, such as Next 20 Nov.
